/-!
# P4-Q2-NJ — genuine SU(2) Wilson kernel sections versus signed dual obstruction

NI: the ACTUAL two-interacting-Wilson-posterior Perron signed Haar
coefficient rho separates every Dirac evaluation on C(SU2,R), with an
explicit genuine positive/negative lobe continuous test.

NH: a nonzero original SU(2) exponential temporal matrix-moment
determinant is equivalent to positive Haar score variance.

NJ constructs a genuine bounded continuous real linear functional
  L_(e,z,c)(f) = integral f(g) rho_(e,z)(g) dHaar(g) - c*f(y),
where y is the ACTUAL right-link boundary z.right(e), and builds the
REAL exponential temporal Wilson kernel sections
  k_x(g) = exp(b * Re(trace(x^{-1}g))/2).
For c=q_(e,z)(1), L(k_x) is EXACTLY NH's normalized character
moment defect. No abstract test is inserted in place of the
physical signed receiver or its real posterior law.

The rigorous unconditional NEW obstruction:
  beta>0 AND Q_(e,z)=0
    => the REAL LINEAR SPAN of {k_x | x in SU(2)}
       is NOT DENSE in C(SU(2),R).
The proof uses NI's proved nonzero original signed functional and
mathlib's extension of equality of continuous linear maps from a
dense span. It introduces NO density axiom, and DOES NOT assert
the required kernel-span density.

Crucial: Stone–Weierstrass density of the ALGEBRA generated by
k_x is NOT by itself density of their LINEAR SPAN, since k_x*k_y
does not generally lie in the fixed-b linear span. The latter is
precisely the outstanding SU(2) harmonic/Bessel coefficient theorem.

No independent Haar posterior, substitute GI detector/source,
assumed rank/injectivity, Dobrushin, sorry or new axioms.
-/

